    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to present No. 20 John Dillon Street, a beautifully presented two-bedroom end-of-terrace red brick residence ideally positioned on this quiet and highly sought-after street in the heart of Dublin 8. Extending to approximately 62 sq.m., this charming home effortlessly combines period character with modern comforts, offering bright, well-proportioned accommodation within walking distance of the city centre.\n\nThe accommodation comprises an inviting open-plan living and dining room, where high ceilings, dual-aspect windows and a feature wood-burning stove create a warm and welcoming atmosphere. Cleverly designed shelving and colourful interiors enhance the sense of space and individuality throughout.\n\nTo the rear, the modern fitted kitchen offers ample storage and worktop space while overlooking the private courtyard garden. A contemporary shower room completes the ground floor accommodation.\n\nUpstairs, there are two generous bedrooms, both filled with natural light. The principal bedroom features attractive exposed brick detailing, while the second bedroom provides an ideal guest room, home office or nursery.\n\nOutside, a low-maintenance enclosed rear courtyard offers a private outdoor retreat perfect for morning coffee or evening relaxation.\n\nSituated in one of Dublin 8's most vibrant neighbourhoods, the property enjoys every conceivable amenity on its doorstep including cafés, restaurants, shops, parks and excellent public transport links. The city centre, The Liberties, St. James's Hospital, Heuston Station and the Phoenix Park are all within easy reach, making this an ideal home for first-time buyers, professionals and investors alike."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Attractive red brick end-of-terrace home</li><li> Bright open-plan living and dining room</li><li> Feature wood-burning stove</li><li> Modern fitted kitchen</li><li> Two well-proportioned bedrooms</li><li> Contemporary shower room</li><li> Gas-fired central heating</li><li> Private, low-maintenance rear courtyard</li><li> Excellent natural light throughout due to end-of-terrace position</li><li> Highly sought-after Dublin 8 location</li><li> Walking distance to the city centre and a host of local amenities</ul>"
      },
